{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-85080" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola $5{x}^{2}+30x+2y+41=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-85080" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of an upward- or downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nTo write the given equation in this form, we need to group the $x$-terms on the left-hand side and complete the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{2}+30x+2y+41 & =0 \\\\ 5{x}^{2}+30x & =-2y-41 \\\\ 5[{x}^{2}+6x] & =-2y-41 \\\\ 5[(x+3)^{2}-9] & =-2y-41 \\\\ 5(x+3)^{2}-45 & =-2y-41 \\\\ 5(x+3)^{2} & =-2y-41+45 \\\\ 5(x+3)^{2} & =-2y+4 \\\\ 5(x+3)^{2} & =-2(y-2) \\\\ (x+3)^{2} & =-\\frac{2}{5}(y-2) \\\\ (x+3)^{2} & =4(-\\frac{1}{10})(y-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the vertex are $(h,k)=(-3,2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-85080" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f6221ff180acafaeaafdf9a9050db5cc20ab72ce4073d30ccfe6cc85ac2a58be"} {"question" "q-85080" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-85080" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-3,2)"] ["math" "(-3,4)"] ["math" "(2,-3)"] ["math" "(2,3)"] ["math" "(3,4)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-85080" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-3,2)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-11884" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola $3{x}^{2}-30x-8y+67=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-11884" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of an upward- or downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nTo write the given equation in this form, we need to group the $x$-terms on the left-hand side and complete the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-30x-8y+67 & =0 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-30x & =8y-67 \\\\ 3[{x}^{2}-10x] & =8y-67 \\\\ 3[(x-5)^{2}-25] & =8y-67 \\\\ 3(x-5)^{2}-75 & =8y-67 \\\\ 3(x-5)^{2} & =8y-67+75 \\\\ 3(x-5)^{2} & =8y+8 \\\\ 3(x-5)^{2} & =8(y+1) \\\\ (x-5)^{2} & =\\frac{8}{3}(y+1) \\\\ (x-5)^{2} & =4(\\frac{2}{3})(y+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the vertex are $(h,k)=(5,-1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-11884" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f6221ff180acafaeaafdf9a9050db5cc20ab72ce4073d30ccfe6cc85ac2a58be"} {"question" "q-11884" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-11884" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-1,5)"] ["math" "(-5,-1)"] ["math" "(1,5)"] ["math" "(5,-1)"] ["math" "(5,1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-11884" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(5,-1)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-11880" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola ${x}^{2}-6x-2y+19=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-11880" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of an upward- or downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nTo write the given equation in this form, we need to group the $x$-terms on the left-hand side and complete the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-6x-2y+19 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-6x & =2y-19 \\\\ (x-3)^{2}-9 & =2y-19 \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =2y-19+9 \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =2y-10 \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =2(y-5) \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =4(\\frac{1}{2})(y-5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the vertex are $(h,k)=(3,5).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-11880" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f6221ff180acafaeaafdf9a9050db5cc20ab72ce4073d30ccfe6cc85ac2a58be"} {"question" "q-11880" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-11880" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-3,-5)"] ["math" "(-5,-3)"] ["math" "(3,5)"] ["math" "(4,5)"] ["math" "(5,3)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-11880" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(3,5)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-103668" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola ${x}^{2}+2x-2y-1=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-103668" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of an upward- or downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nTo write the given equation in this form, we need to group the $x$-terms on the left-hand side and complete the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2x-2y-1 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2x & =2y+1 \\\\ (x+1)^{2}-1 & =2y+1 \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =2y+1+1 \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =2y+2 \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =4(\\frac{1}{2})(y+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the vertex are $(h,k)=(-1,-1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-103668" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f6221ff180acafaeaafdf9a9050db5cc20ab72ce4073d30ccfe6cc85ac2a58be"} {"question" "q-103668" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-103668" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-1,-1)"] ["math" "(-1,1)"] ["math" "(-2,1)"] ["math" "(1,1)"] ["math" "(2,-1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-103668" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-1,-1)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-11883" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola $3{x}^{2}+6x+4y+15=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-11883" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of an upward- or downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nTo write the given equation in this form, we need to group the $x$-terms on the left-hand side and complete the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+6x+4y+15 & =0 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}+6x & =-4y-15 \\\\ 3[{x}^{2}+2x] & =-4y-15 \\\\ 3[(x+1)^{2}-1] & =-4y-15 \\\\ 3(x+1)^{2}-3 & =-4y-15 \\\\ 3(x+1)^{2} & =-4y-15+3 \\\\ 3(x+1)^{2} & =-4y-12 \\\\ 3(x+1)^{2} & =-4(y+3) \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =-\\frac{4}{3}(y+3) \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =4(-\\frac{1}{3})(y+3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the vertex are $(h,k)=(-1,-3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-11883" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f6221ff180acafaeaafdf9a9050db5cc20ab72ce4073d30ccfe6cc85ac2a58be"} {"question" "q-11883" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-11883" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-1,-3)"] ["math" "(-1,3)"] ["math" "(-3,-1)"] ["math" "(1,3)"] ["math" "(3,-1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-11883" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-1,-3)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-103679" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola ${y}^{2}-8x-2y+33=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-103679" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nTo write the given equation in this form, we need to group the $y$-terms on the left-hand side and complete the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-8x-2y+33 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}-2y & =8x-33 \\\\ (y-1)^{2}-1 & =8x-33 \\\\ (y-1)^{2} & =8x-33+1 \\\\ (y-1)^{2} & =8x-32 \\\\ (y-1)^{2} & =8(x-4) \\\\ (y-1)^{2} & =4(2)(x-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the vertex are $(h,k)=(4,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-103679" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f6221ff180acafaeaafdf9a9050db5cc20ab72ce4073d30ccfe6cc85ac2a58be"} {"question" "q-103679" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-103679" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-2,3)"] ["math" "(1,-5)"] ["math" "(2,-3)"] ["math" "(2,-4)"] ["math" "(4,1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-103679" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(4,1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-86523" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola $3{y}^{2}-2x+18y+29=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-86523" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nTo write the given equation in this form, we need to group the $y$-terms on the left-hand side and complete the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2}-2x+18y+29 & =0 \\\\ 3{y}^{2}+18y & =2x-29 \\\\ 3[{y}^{2}+6y] & =2x-29 \\\\ 3[(y+3)^{2}-9] & =2x-29 \\\\ 3(y+3)^{2}-27 & =2x-29 \\\\ 3(y+3)^{2} & =2x-29+27 \\\\ 3(y+3)^{2} & =2x-2 \\\\ 3(y+3)^{2} & =2(x-1) \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =\\frac{2}{3}(x-1) \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =4(\\frac{1}{6})(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the vertex are $(h,k)=(1,-3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-86523" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f6221ff180acafaeaafdf9a9050db5cc20ab72ce4073d30ccfe6cc85ac2a58be"} {"question" "q-86523" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-86523" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-3,-1)"] ["math" "(-3,2)"] ["math" "(1,-3)"] ["math" "(2,-3)"] ["math" "(3,-1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-86523" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(1,-3)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-103677" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola $2{y}^{2}-x+4y=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-103677" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nTo write the given equation in this form, we need to group the $y$-terms on the left-hand side and complete the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{2}-x+4y & =0 \\\\ 2{y}^{2}+4y & =x \\\\ 2[{y}^{2}+2y] & =x \\\\ 2[(y+1)^{2}-1] & =x \\\\ 2(y+1)^{2}-2 & =x \\\\ 2(y+1)^{2} & =x+2 \\\\ (y+1)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}(x+2) \\\\ (y+1)^{2} & =4(\\frac{1}{8})(x+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the vertex are $(h,k)=(-2,-1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063652/state.json" "file_sha256" "7626fb3aadf54178c3dab5c6dae5c454714220bb44f31faaeaae6744128c066f"} {"question" "q-103677" "field" nil "attribute" "question/diffi